{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3d487f157fa9c38f65f19c90f7d8b5624c9d8e739860fff0ed6459160dfe44da"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product exposes a CLI including `ocx init`, `start`, `stop`, `service`, `codex-shim install`, `health`, `ready`, `status`, `gui`, plus subcommands for providers, accounts, combos, and v2 surface controls."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3f420b19841d6e0c6f7fa840ccfc05c25f8038b0cf85495c69bc5369fb7c9f1c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The proxy can manage a ChatGPT account pool for Codex auth: quota-aware routing sends new sessions to the lowest-usage healthy account under quota policy, while existing threads normally keep affinity to their starting account, with rebinding on failover, exclusion, affinity expiry, or 401/403/429 recovery."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4693d1cbb9ea8aaa67cc8aab0d05126d48132d4c15fb33e37ca2106285c5dab6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The management API refuses agent-driven star requests with `403 agent_consent_required`, and the CLI suppresses the interactive star prompt when an agent is detected, leaving the decision to the user."},{"claim_ids":["clm_574a4a9d05c6adc6cee83da3237d13974a067c6eead44a672081af1c207e9bfd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Combos provide a single virtual model id with failover or weighted round-robin across providers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5e4e3312513e7689faceaf727c36469b390712f4042e6640005fdef7df813732"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Models are targeted with a `provider/model` syntax (e.g. `codex -m \"anthropic/claude-opus-5\"`); omitting the prefix uses the default provider or name-pattern auto-matching, and inner slashes in provider model ids are aliased to `-`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7cd40746fdc8c97761169b413aa712e807933bf95f18a882b3228b51084b9d72"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: source development requires the bun CLI on PATH (separate from the bundled runtime), and contributors run `bun install`, `bun run typecheck`, and `bun run test`; contributor setup lives in CONTRIBUTING.md."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8e15bb6a783e8b1e534381dc9458c5e65d563b6c43a9634ee2555f091ffffdd4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"By default the proxy binds to 127.0.0.1 without authentication; binding beyond loopback requires OPENCODEX_API_AUTH_TOKEN, which every client request must carry as the `x-opencodex-api-key` header."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9f4a7a386e93bbe17d59a42945df75697074332dfb854400cce04978625fbc62"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The package requires Node 18+ and bundles the Bun runtime on npm install, so no separate Bun installation (or WSL on Windows) is needed; supported OSes are macOS, Linux, and Windows x64 with launchd, systemd user units, or Task Scheduler/WinSW respectively."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ace621e3a99791d266c18fbe2e8437a97b2aa7bfda5e41018b2b6228ebbe9e43"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The runtime tracks 36 categories of retained process state: 12 byte-accounted stores evicted under a default 256 MiB budget, 4 monitored buffers, 24 state-store registrations with 60s expiry sweeps, and LRU-capped memos; live bytes are inspectable via GET /api/system/memory with the admin token."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e051d2f06c9c6681665a728e2c1e7938c74947be8a01a3bd78a219813f39afea"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project warns it is community-maintained and unaffiliated with OpenAI or Anthropic, and that providers such as Anthropic may suspend accounts routing through third-party proxies, so use is at the user's own risk."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f191ab9b9bf78fe94c2d944c012709b165babae3cd0b3163c6e102e2c9493375"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The proxy serves `GET /healthz` for liveness and an unauthenticated `GET /readyz` returning a sanitized JSON identity; ready returns 200 while pending/failed return 503 with Retry-After: 1."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3d487f157fa9c38f65f19c90f7d8b5624c9d8e739860fff0ed6459160dfe44da","clm_3f420b19841d6e0c6f7fa840ccfc05c25f8038b0cf85495c69bc5369fb7c9f1c","clm_4693d1cbb9ea8aaa67cc8aab0d05126d48132d4c15fb33e37ca2106285c5dab6","clm_574a4a9d05c6adc6cee83da3237d13974a067c6eead44a672081af1c207e9bfd","clm_5e4e3312513e7689faceaf727c36469b390712f4042e6640005fdef7df813732","clm_7cd40746fdc8c97761169b413aa712e807933bf95f18a882b3228b51084b9d72","clm_8e15bb6a783e8b1e534381dc9458c5e65d563b6c43a9634ee2555f091ffffdd4","clm_9f4a7a386e93bbe17d59a42945df75697074332dfb854400cce04978625fbc62","clm_ace621e3a99791d266c18fbe2e8437a97b2aa7bfda5e41018b2b6228ebbe9e43","clm_e051d2f06c9c6681665a728e2c1e7938c74947be8a01a3bd78a219813f39afea","clm_f191ab9b9bf78fe94c2d944c012709b165babae3cd0b3163c6e102e2c9493375"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102","id":"pg_4096a469f8a95d2cacf138f944462a41","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/lidge-jun-opencodex-readme-md-9f7397ed1582-38f944462a41.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_a158f48d66a65c32b7711029e4a77da5"],"title":"lidge-jun/opencodex/README.md @ 9f7397ed1582","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_702709e4a1e295802072691dd637512dd7591828f2785eb8c77794f8de98ffb7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Integration with Codex works by writing Codex-native config and catalog files under CODEX_HOME (config.toml, opencodex.config.toml, opencodex-catalog.json, models_cache.json), so routed models appear in Codex's picker without patching Codex itself."}],"claim_ids":["clm_702709e4a1e295802072691dd637512dd7591828f2785eb8c77794f8de98ffb7"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102","id":"pg_4368218df17d5b20b44d0b11f292457e","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/lidge-jun-opencodex-docs-codex-app-model-catalog-md-9f7397ed1582-0b11f292457e.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_8a3bad3f83415e2ead5c829da034247f"],"title":"lidge-jun/opencodex/docs/codex-app-model-catalog.md @ 9f7397ed1582","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102"}
